{
 "about": [
  "Who may sign what is itself a signed lock. A signer is the claims on `keys/<id>`: class, public key,",
  "coverage (scope prefixes) and resolution (scope depths). The root of the tree admits one signer; every",
  "other signer is admitted when a quorum of admitted authorize signers signed its class.",
  "",
  "It got its own file because one owner key was hardcoded, and 16 `audit/step` lines that said by=owner",
  "carried authority on 2026-09-17 although no key in the tree verified them. Such a line is grey.",
  "",
  "`verify` here is a stand-in so the vector needs no keys: a line verifies against a public key when its",
  "`sig` is `ok:` followed by that key. The host adapter verifies real signatures."
 ],
 "verify": "sig === 'ok:' + publicKey",
 "root": {
  "id": "owner",
  "keyClass": "authorize",
  "publicKey": "K0",
  "coverage": [
   "*"
  ],
  "depth": {
   "lo": 1,
   "hi": 16
  },
  "admittedBy": []
 },
